Fix frontend HTTP verbs against Edge Functions (Task #922)

The contract matrix flagged frontend call sites that POSTed to handlers
which only consult URL query params/headers, never the request body.
While Supabase's invoke layer accepted these calls, they were
semantically wrong and risked breaking under stricter validation.

Changes:
- src/hooks/useCurrencyConversion.ts: fx-rates fetch switched POST → GET
  and the unused `body: "null"` / Content-Type removed.
- src/repositories/payments.repository.ts: `invokeFXRate` rewritten to
  send GET with query params (matches the fx-rates handler contract).
- src/services/data/forex-data-service.ts: invoke fx-rates with
  `{ method: "GET" }` instead of `{ body: null }`.
- src/lib/engines/backend-connectivity-engine.ts: health-check probe
  switched to `{ method: "GET" }` (handler ignores body).
- src/pages/admin/AdminDldBackfillPage.tsx: dld-analytics
  `backfill-status` (read) switched to GET; `backfill` (mutation) kept
  POST and now also includes a body for parity with intent.
- supabase/functions/_contracts.ts: `health-check` declared methods
  changed from ["POST"] to ["GET"] to reflect the only real caller and
  the GET-style handler semantics.
- docs/edge-functions-contract-matrix.{md,json}: regenerated.

Verification:
  npx tsx scripts/edge-function-contract-matrix.ts --ci
  ✓ 257 call sites · 0 method/body/auth/orphan mismatches.

Note: usePaymentFX.ts was listed in the task but already used GET; no
edits needed.

